  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional Commercialization Support Phase 2 (ACTS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of phase II of this project is to strengthen and streamline the systems and processes within the selected institutions (from phase 1) towards successful commercialisation of their research outputs with a desired outcome of promoting innovation to drive job creation, increase employability, and social-economic growth. The specific objectives of this project are: 
a. Development and identification of relevant criteria to select first four (4) institutions to operationalize the interventions from Phase I and those proposed in phase II. 
b. Co-development of a practical implementation plan for each of the institutions to guide recommended interventions 
c. Support the institutions to implement interventions for commercialization systems in a pragmatic, sustainable and inclusive way 
d. Co-organize stakeholder consultations for networking, learning to draw out key lessons for wider dissemination across institutions 
e. Support the development of an M&amp;E framework to be used by KeNIA and the respective institutions to keep the TTOs well supervised and accountable.</narrative>
  </description>
